desc:Spaced Tetrahedral Ambisonic Encoder 10oA
// =============================================================================
// Spaced Tetrahedral Ambisonic Encoder
// =============================================================================
// 4 mono inputs -> ambisonic bus (1OA..10OA), ambiX (ACN+SN3D) by default
//
// Array presets:
//
//   STAND-MOUNT (Ch3 straight down, stand mounts from Ch3 side):
//     Ch1 (Thumb)  : az +120  el +19.4712   (Back-Left-Up)
//     Ch2 (Index)  : az    0  el +19.4712   (Forward-Up)
//     Ch3 (Middle) : az    0  el -90        (Straight Down)
//     Ch4 (Ring)   : az -120  el +19.4712   (Back-Right-Up)
//
//   ALT-AZIMUTH (upper pair front/back, lower pair left/right):
//     Ch1 (Thumb)  : az +180  el +35.26     (Back-Up)
//     Ch2 (Index)  : az    0  el +35.26     (Forward-Up)
//     Ch3 (Middle) : az  +90  el -35.26     (Right-Down)
//     Ch4 (Ring)   : az  -90  el -35.26     (Left-Down)
//
//   CUSTOM:
//     User-defined per-channel azimuth and elevation via sliders.
//
// All three presets produce regular tetrahedra (pairwise dot product = -1/3).
//
// Source modes:
//   Outside-In : virtual source placed at the mic's physical position
//   Inside-Out : virtual source placed at the antipode (field radiates outward)
//
// Output channel count:
//   1OA = 4,   2OA = 9,    3OA = 16,   4OA = 25,   5OA = 36,
//   6OA = 49,  7OA = 64,   8OA = 81,   9OA = 100,  10OA = 121
// Set the track to a matching channel count.
//
// NOTE on enum sliders: JSFX stores the 0-indexed position of the selected
// dropdown entry regardless of declared min. `ambi_order = s_order + 1`.
// =============================================================================

